{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/629717-a-little-alt-history","id":629717,"title":"A little alt history.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-17T02:29:58-07:00","id":629717,"title":"A little alt history.","content":"<i>This story is true. In the time before, when Man was still screaming their birth cries into the night, there were brother spirits who wanted to be more than they were, so they came to each other for council. \u201cOnly though domination is strength known,\u201d said the eldest. \u201cThe ability to survive any difficulty makes one strong,\u201d said the second. This argument went on for many years, each of the brother spirits attempted to display how his strength should be the measure of all strength, for if that was known then the brother spirits would become mighty indeed.<br /> <br /> After a time of this, the youngest and cleverest of the brother spirits spoke, \u201cBrothers,\u201d it said to the surrounding growls, for as the youngest he had not yet earned to right to speak during council, \u201cFor many ages we have argued the same point with no real end in sight. Come see what I have seen, for this may hold a way to true strength.\u201d Curiosity teased, the other spirit brothers loped after the youngest.<br /> <br /> The youngest showed his brother spirits a thing they had not before seen. A group of skin changers who were also part spirit! \u201cI shall teach them to dominate,\u201d said Dire Wolf. \u201cI shall teach them to endure,\u201d said Winter Wolf. And so on until it came to the youngest. \u201cI shall teach them cunning,\u201d said Red Wolf. </i><br /> <br /> A little alternate history that I wrote up. I thought it was kind of odd that of all the &quot;main&quot; splats Werewolf was the only one with an absolute origin that 